# 6. DODGE SYSTEM

## 6.1 Purpose

Dodge gives the player a short defensive movement action to avoid an in-game guard encounter.

It is not an attack mechanic.

## 6.2 Controls

Desktop: `Shift`

Mobile: dedicated Dodge button.

## 6.3 Initial Parameters

| Parameter | Initial value |
|---|---:|
| Dodge duration | 0.25 seconds |
| Cooldown | 2.0 seconds |
| Movement distance | Approximately 2 world units |
| Temporary contact protection | 0.3 seconds |
| Input | Current movement direction |

These are gameplay tuning values and may be adjusted during testing.

## 6.4 Dodge Rules

- Dodge follows the player's current movement direction.
- If no movement direction is held, use a short backward dodge.
- Dodge must respect wall collision.
- Dodge must not move through locked doors.
- Dodge must not move through environmental obstacles.
- Dodge has a visible cooldown indicator.
- The player cannot spam dodge continuously.
- Dodge does not cause damage to enemies.
- Dodge does not provide a weapon or attack action.

If a guard contact occurs during the brief protection window, the catch event is ignored.

The feature must remain a fictional in-game movement mechanic.

