# 12. SCORING AND GAME PROGRESSION

## 12.1 Lives

Starting lives: 5.

- Wrong answers on quiz doors do not remove lives.
- Wrong or timed-out quick guard questions remove one life.
- Three consecutive correct answers restore one life.
- Maximum lives: 5.

## 12.2 Score

Preserve the original scoring model as the starting point:

Score = (Correct × 100) + (Keys × 150) + (Remaining Lives × 50) + (Best Streak × 20) − (Wrong × 30) + (Win Bonus 400).

Rank:

| Rank | Score |
|---|---:|
| S | 1700+ |
| A | 1300+ |
| B | 950+ |
| C | 650+ |
| D | 380+ |
| E | Below 380 |

Review the rank thresholds after balancing the new maze.

## 12.3 Victory

The player wins by:
1. Collecting all five keys.
2. Unlocking the three escape routes.
3. Reaching any one of the three valid exit locations.

The victory screen displays:
- Completion time.
- Final score.
- Rank.
- Remaining lives.
- Keys collected.
- Correct and incorrect answers.
- Best streak.
- Dodge count.
- Selected escape route.

## 12.4 Game Over

Game Over occurs when the player's lives reach zero.

Provide:
- Retry.
- Main Menu.
- Result summary.

