# 14. PERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS

The project is a browser-based 3D game. Rendering performance is important.

Requirements:
- Use InstancedMesh for repeated wall and floor meshes where practical.
- Avoid creating thousands of separate draw calls.
- Use small texture files.
- Use nearest filtering for pixel textures.
- Limit dynamic lights.
- Avoid unnecessary real-time shadows.
- Use delta time for movement and animation.
- Dispose of unused geometry and materials.
- Do not rebuild the entire maze every frame.
- Use efficient collision and pathfinding.

Initial targets:
- 60 FPS on a reasonable desktop browser.
- 30 FPS minimum target on tested lower-performance devices.
- Stable gameplay after opening and closing quiz panels.
- No memory leak from repeated game restarts.

Provide quality settings:
- Low.
- Medium.
- High.

