| `nearDoor()` | 3D proximity/raycast interaction |
| Canvas minimap | Hand-drawn HTML minimap |
| localStorage save | Versioned localStorage save |
| Web Audio | AudioManager using Web Audio API |
| Old BANK | WWII question data |
| Old MONSTER_BANK | Quick True/False pool or filtered shared question bank |
| Score calculation | Adapted ScoreManager |
| Settings | New SettingsManager |

## 16.3 Old Validation to Replace

The old question validator expects:
- 240 questions in the main bank.
- 40 questions in the monster bank.
- Six unrelated school subject categories.

These validation rules must be removed.

Replace them with the new requirement:
- 24 multiple-choice questions.
- 16 true/false questions.
- Six WWII categories.
- Valid answer and explanation.
- Source references.
- Unique question IDs.

Do not leave old mathematics or other unrelated subjects inside the game.

## 16.4 Rendering Migration

The old `draw()` function is Canvas 2D and must not remain the primary world renderer.

Create a real Three.js scene.

Required:
- Scene.
- Perspective camera.
- WebGL renderer.
- Floor meshes.
- Wall meshes.
- Door meshes.
- Key meshes.
- Guard models.
- Environment props.
- Lighting.

Use the 64×64 maze array as the source of world geometry.

A grid cell maps to a 3D world position.

```text
Grid coordinate:
(x, y)

3D world:
(x * cellSize, 0, y * cellSize)
```

Keep map data separate from meshes.

The same grid data must be used by:
- Renderer.
- Player collision.
- Guard pathfinding.
- Minimap.
- Route validation.
- Collectible placement.

## 16.5 Preserve Legacy Reference

Do not delete or overwrite the original HTML file.

Create a separate legacy backup:

```text
legacy/
